WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.438
Unit 3 is domain controllers.

2
00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:07.550
The program retires its domain controllers;
until then, they're Tier zero.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.236
Learn's procedure: publish the
D C's on T C P eighty-eight,

4
00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:16.263
in Quick Access or an app, and name
the service principal names to protect.

5
00:00:16.263 --> 00:00:20.612
Open inbound T C P thirteen
thirty-seven on the D C's.

6
00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:25.463
Install one sensor per D C, silently,
and register it with a token.

7
00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:27.771
The sensor installs in Audit mode,

8
00:00:27.771 --> 00:00:31.400
so you read its event log
before anything is enforced.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.746
Learn's advice is to test with
application S P N's first,

10
00:00:35.746 --> 00:00:40.684
and protect the D C's own S P N
only later, to avoid admin lockout,

11
00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:44.338
and to assess N T L M use
before restricting it.

12
00:00:44.338 --> 00:00:48.723
The rollback is the sensor's
break-glass mode, from the admin center,

13
00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:52.312
or a registry value set to
one and the sensor restarted.

14
00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:55.078
And the registration
token is a credential:

15
00:00:55.078 --> 00:01:00.220
acquire it on a privileged access workstation,
use it once, and clear the session.
